WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.467 --> 00:00:03.569
-Thank you very much.
Welcome to "The Tonight Show."

00:00:03.569 --> 00:00:04.603
My name is Jimmy Fallon.

00:00:04.603 --> 00:00:06.139
And that's the Roots
right over there.

00:00:06.139 --> 00:00:08.675
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:08.675 --> 00:00:10.643
Well, guys,
as I mentioned earlier,

00:00:10.643 --> 00:00:13.646
Ruth Bader Ginsburg's passing
dominated the news this weekend.

00:00:13.646 --> 00:00:15.915
Even President Trump
seemed genuinely saddened

00:00:15.915 --> 00:00:17.083
when he heard about it.

00:00:17.083 --> 00:00:18.751
Actually you thought
we were finally seeing

00:00:18.751 --> 00:00:20.519
a more empathetic Trump
until he addressed

00:00:20.519 --> 00:00:24.524
the open Supreme Court seat
at his rally 24 hours later.

00:00:24.524 --> 00:00:29.428
-So, I have to make a decision
to fill the seat, as we say.

00:00:29.428 --> 00:00:30.696
We should have a new campaign.

00:00:30.696 --> 00:00:33.566
Let's make a T-shirt --
"Fill the Seat," okay?

00:00:33.566 --> 00:00:37.036
[ Crowd chanting ]

00:00:37.036 --> 00:00:40.940
That's a -- That's a good idea.
Fill the seat.

00:00:40.940 --> 00:00:42.241
-Wow.

00:00:42.241 --> 00:00:43.976
Man, when you see that,
it's hard to believe Trump

00:00:43.976 --> 00:00:45.578
hasn't been asked
to give the eulogy.

00:00:45.578 --> 00:00:47.713
[ Laughter ]

00:00:47.713 --> 00:00:50.183
Trump could be somber for about
15 seconds, then he's like,

00:00:50.183 --> 00:00:52.118
"You think they'll have
Bagel Bites at the reception?"

00:00:52.118 --> 00:00:53.119
[ Laughter ]

00:00:53.119 --> 00:00:54.254
What is he doing?

00:00:54.254 --> 00:00:55.622
Why do all of his rallies --

00:00:55.622 --> 00:00:57.089
Why do they all have chants?

00:00:57.089 --> 00:00:59.425
He's the President,
not the host of an infomercial.

00:00:59.425 --> 00:01:01.227
Fry that chicken!

00:01:01.227 --> 00:01:05.131
[ Laughter ]

00:01:05.131 --> 00:01:08.568
You don't want a room of people
chanting during a pandemic.

00:01:08.568 --> 00:01:10.936
Seriously, at that point, even
the coronavirus puts on his coat

00:01:10.936 --> 00:01:12.872
and was like, "I don't want to
be part of this, okay?

00:01:12.872 --> 00:01:14.841
Good day to you."

00:01:14.841 --> 00:01:16.909
But if you thought
Trump was joking,

00:01:16.909 --> 00:01:19.112
look at what popped up on
his website over the weekend.

00:01:20.146 --> 00:01:22.748
Yeah, the Trump campaign
is now selling

00:01:22.748 --> 00:01:24.918
"fill that seat" T-shirts.

00:01:24.918 --> 00:01:27.887
Seriously, someone just passed
away and he's leading chants

00:01:27.887 --> 00:01:29.888
and selling T-shirts
like they just clinched

00:01:29.888 --> 00:01:31.724
the American League East.

00:01:31.724 --> 00:01:33.893
When people said
it was in bad taste,

00:01:33.893 --> 00:01:35.260
Trump was like, "Good call.

00:01:35.260 --> 00:01:38.865
Let's also print out some
college shirts, class it up."

00:01:38.865 --> 00:01:40.766
Here's some advice -- If you're
wondering how to deal with

00:01:40.766 --> 00:01:43.035
a job opening after someone dies
and you find yourself

00:01:43.035 --> 00:01:45.972
on a custom T-shirt website,
you made a wrong turn.

00:01:45.972 --> 00:01:48.274
[ Laughter ]

00:01:48.274 --> 00:01:50.977
Even long-haul drivers
with truck nuts were like,

00:01:50.977 --> 00:01:52.478
"That's just
crude and unnecessary."

00:01:52.478 --> 00:01:54.913
[ Laughter ]

00:01:54.913 --> 00:01:57.617
But it's true. Trump is hoping
to fill the seat soon

00:01:57.617 --> 00:01:59.118
and he even offered some details

00:01:59.118 --> 00:02:01.654
on who he's thinking about
filling it with.

00:02:01.654 --> 00:02:04.657
-I will be putting forth
a nominee next week.

00:02:04.657 --> 00:02:07.293
It will be a woman.

00:02:07.293 --> 00:02:09.228
-Trump said that
like he was announcing

00:02:09.228 --> 00:02:10.930
the gender of
the next royal baby.

00:02:10.930 --> 00:02:12.031
[ Laughter ]

00:02:12.031 --> 00:02:15.368
"Hear ye, hear ye,
it will be a woman."

00:02:15.368 --> 00:02:16.769
[ Laughter ]

00:02:16.769 --> 00:02:18.938
This is actually good news
because usually when you hear

00:02:18.938 --> 00:02:21.007
"Trump, judge," and "woman"
in the same sentence,

00:02:21.007 --> 00:02:22.375
it's because he's
being sued again.

00:02:22.375 --> 00:02:23.609
[ Laughter ]

00:02:23.609 --> 00:02:25.211
And this morning
on "Fox &amp; Friends,"

00:02:25.211 --> 00:02:27.914
Trump was asked if he knew which
day he'd announce the nominee.

00:02:27.914 --> 00:02:28.948
Watch this.

00:02:46.999 --> 00:02:49.001
"That's right.
We want to be very respectful.

00:02:49.001 --> 00:02:51.170
I even asked Kid Rock to record
an acoustic version

00:02:51.170 --> 00:02:53.239
of 'Bawitdaba' to be played
during the funeral."

00:02:53.239 --> 00:02:54.373
[ Laughter ]

00:02:54.373 --> 00:02:55.975
Yeah, they're trying
to be respectful.

00:02:55.975 --> 00:02:58.544
That's why for the next hour
Trump's knocking 20% off

00:02:58.544 --> 00:03:00.980
all "fill that seat"
merchandise, so act now!

00:03:00.980 --> 00:03:02.347
[ Laughter ]

00:03:02.347 --> 00:03:04.550
Trump is being very respectful,
but when asked about

00:03:04.550 --> 00:03:06.752
Justice Ginsburg's dying wish
for the next president

00:03:06.752 --> 00:03:08.988
to choose her successor,
here's what he had to say.

00:03:25.771 --> 00:03:27.206
Well, that was
an interesting way

00:03:27.206 --> 00:03:29.308
of paying respects, wasn't it?

00:03:29.308 --> 00:03:31.310
Over the weekend,
Republican senators like

00:03:31.310 --> 00:03:33.412
Ted Cruz, Mitch McConnell,
and Lindsey Graham

00:03:33.412 --> 00:03:36.148
said they plan to move forward
with a vote on Trump's nominee.

00:03:36.148 --> 00:03:39.319
However, that contradicts
what they said back in 2016

00:03:39.319 --> 00:03:41.820
when President Obama
nominated Merrick Garland

00:03:41.820 --> 00:03:43.188
close to an election.

00:03:43.188 --> 00:03:44.290
Listen to this.

00:03:44.290 --> 00:03:45.825 line:0%
-There is a long tradition

00:03:45.825 --> 00:03:47.627 line:0%
that you don't do this
in an election year.

00:03:47.627 --> 00:03:51.096 line:0%
-The Senate will appropriately
revisit the matter

00:03:51.096 --> 00:03:54.467 line:0%
when it considers the
qualifications of the nominee

00:03:54.467 --> 00:03:57.370 line:0%
the next President nominates.

00:03:57.370 --> 00:03:59.639 line:0%
-I want you to use
my words against me.

00:03:59.639 --> 00:04:02.374 line:0%
If there's a Republican
President in 2016

00:04:02.374 --> 00:04:05.878 line:0%
and a vacancy occurs in
the last year of the first term,

00:04:05.878 --> 00:04:09.682 line:0%
you can say Lindsey Graham said
"Let's let the next president,

00:04:09.682 --> 00:04:13.619 line:0%
whoever it might be,
make that nomination."

00:04:13.619 --> 00:04:15.488
-Sure, the Olympics
were canceled this year,

00:04:15.488 --> 00:04:17.089
but at least we have
the Republicans to show off

00:04:17.089 --> 00:04:18.925
some truly spectacular
backflips.

00:04:18.925 --> 00:04:20.592
[ Laughter ]

00:04:20.592 --> 00:04:23.128
Republicans are just constantly
changing the rules as they go.

00:04:23.128 --> 00:04:24.830
It's like playing a board game
with a toddler.

00:04:24.830 --> 00:04:27.300
It's like, "I rolled a two
and I'm wearing blue, so I win."

00:04:27.300 --> 00:04:29.134
[ Laughter ]

00:04:29.134 --> 00:04:31.670
And now, because he completely
changed his position,

00:04:31.670 --> 00:04:34.307
people are calling
Mitch McConnell spineless.

00:04:34.307 --> 00:04:36.309
Can we see Mitch McConnell?

00:04:36.309 --> 00:04:40.045
[ Laughter ]

00:04:40.045 --> 00:04:42.482
Spineless? Based on that,
I'm pretty sure he's boneless.

00:04:42.482 --> 00:04:44.050
[ Laughter ]

00:04:44.050 --> 00:04:46.418
We're already in the middle of
a global pandemic,

00:04:46.418 --> 00:04:49.088
racial unrest,
and a cratering economy.

00:04:49.088 --> 00:04:51.858
Now there's going to be a fight
over an open Supreme Court seat.

00:04:51.858 --> 00:04:53.325
At this rate, next week's debate

00:04:53.325 --> 00:04:55.528
will be about how to handle
the current alien invasion.

00:04:55.528 --> 00:04:56.728
[ Laughter ]

00:04:56.728 --> 00:04:58.664
2020 really is insane.

00:04:58.664 --> 00:04:59.965
To put things in perspective,

00:04:59.965 --> 00:05:02.468
the biggest news of 2019
was baby Yoda.

00:05:02.468 --> 00:05:03.770
[ Laughter ]

00:05:03.770 --> 00:05:05.170
Seriously,
this election already felt

00:05:05.170 --> 00:05:06.639
like a tense Thanksgiving
dinner.

00:05:06.639 --> 00:05:09.041
Now it's like your uncle just
rolled in straight from rehab.

00:05:09.041 --> 00:05:12.411
[ Laughter ]

00:05:12.411 --> 00:05:13.780
Trump says he'll announce

00:05:13.780 --> 00:05:15.948
his Supreme Court pick
Friday or Saturday.

00:05:15.948 --> 00:05:17.983
Before he does that, though,
he's been calling up

00:05:17.983 --> 00:05:20.453
all the finalists to let them
know they didn't get the job.

00:05:20.453 --> 00:05:22.254
Check out this leaked audio.

00:05:22.254 --> 00:05:24.924 line:0%
-Ted, I can't have someone
on the Supreme Court

00:05:24.924 --> 00:05:26.259 line:0%
with a beard like yours.

00:05:26.259 --> 00:05:28.561 line:0%
You look like a college freshman
who's experimenting with

00:05:28.561 --> 00:05:29.962 line:0%
his look over winter break,

00:05:29.962 --> 00:05:32.264 line:0%
but even a college freshman
knows to shave it off

00:05:32.264 --> 00:05:34.333 line:0%
when the selfie
doesn't get enough likes.

00:05:34.333 --> 00:05:36.435 line:0%
Son, I love you,
but we can't have someone

00:05:36.435 --> 00:05:38.270 line:0%
on the Supreme Court
who has the same energy

00:05:38.270 --> 00:05:40.038 line:0%
as a guy who offers you cocaine

00:05:40.038 --> 00:05:42.108 line:0%
in the bathroom of
a Buffalo Wild Wings.

00:05:42.108 --> 00:05:44.811 line:0%
I just think those robes would
be too heavy on you, Jared.

00:05:44.811 --> 00:05:46.745 line:0%
Put them on and you'll crumble
to the floor

00:05:46.745 --> 00:05:48.347 line:0%
like the Witch
from "Wizard of Oz."

00:05:48.347 --> 00:05:50.482 line:0%
MyPillow guy, you are maybe

00:05:50.482 --> 00:05:53.952 line:0%
the smartest person who has ever
lived, besides me.

00:05:53.952 --> 00:05:55.854 line:0%
And I think that you could have
made a wonderful judge,

00:05:55.854 --> 00:05:58.324 line:0%
presiding over some wonderful
pillow-based cases,

00:05:58.324 --> 00:06:00.826 line:0%
but unfortunately you're --
how should I put this? --

00:06:00.826 --> 00:06:03.028 line:0%
a borderline insane man.

00:06:03.028 --> 00:06:05.197 line:0%
Hey, me, it's me calling.

00:06:05.197 --> 00:06:08.066 line:0%
Hello. I love what you do.
Big fan. Likewise.

00:06:08.066 --> 00:06:09.936 line:0%
I think you're the most
qualified person on Earth

00:06:09.936 --> 00:06:11.103 line:0%
to be on the Supreme Court.

00:06:11.103 --> 00:06:14.440 line:0%
Wow, what an honor to be
nominated by you, me.

00:06:14.440 --> 00:06:16.008
[ Laughter ]

00:06:16.008 --> 00:06:18.977
-And finally, the most important
thing Americans can do is vote,

00:06:18.977 --> 00:06:21.047
and it looks like we're
getting some help from somewhere

00:06:21.047 --> 00:06:22.814
you wouldn't expect. Watch this.

00:06:22.814 --> 00:06:25.050
-Foot Locker is turning
thousands of their stores

00:06:25.050 --> 00:06:26.885
into voter-registration sites

00:06:26.885 --> 00:06:28.854
just six weeks
before the election.

00:06:28.854 --> 00:06:30.456
-It's perfect
'cause when a fight breaks out,

00:06:30.456 --> 00:06:32.725
there will be 40 people dressed
like referees to handle it.

